ugustin","id":14001491,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MDAxNDkx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14001491?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohdearaugustin","html_url":"https://github.com/ohdearaugustin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohdearaugustin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohdearaugustin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohdearaugustin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohdearaugustin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohdearaugustin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohdearaugustin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohdearaugustin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohdearaugustin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohdearaugustin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Further more I would like to open up a discussion here if it is not maybe a better idea to use setting defaults in viper to make a runable version of headscale. Adding the functionality of init would make it even harder to run headscale without the need of config file.\r\n\r\nI would love to be able to configure headscale just via environment vars. which would make it even easier to run it with kubernetes or other containerization. As you mentioned Vagrant it would also be a nice way to configure headscale their only via environment vars making the whole app more selfcontained.\r\n\r\nHope this is not the wrong place for those thoughts.","commit_id":"09ec217bb1c5b28339acfce2038fe1fa462a6b0d","state":"commented","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/57#pullrequestreview-714265671","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/pulls/57","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/57#pullrequestreview-714265671"},"pull_request":