/viq","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viq/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viq/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viq/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viq/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viq/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viq/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viq/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viq/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/viq/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-07-25T18:05:12Z","updated_at":"2021-07-25T18:05:12Z","body":"Not that there's much secrets in configuration besides the database\npassword, but oftentimes files are easier to keep secret than environment\nof a process, so if possible I'd rather keep the ability to feed it a\nconfig file.\n\nOn Sun, 25 Jul 2021, 18:24 Juan Font, ***@***.***> wrote:\n\n> @cure <https://github.com/cure> @ohdearaugustin\n> <https://github.com/ohdearaugustin>\n>\n> You are very right. I do agree that the idea of this PR makes sense, and\n> its quite convenient (in particular removing the need for wireguard-tools\n> to be installed to generate the wg key). However, how the configuration is\n> defined in a string + removing the check on a valid config at Headscale\n> start is suboptimal / crap 😅\n>\n> I do agree with @ohdearaugustin <https://github.com/ohdearaugustin> on\n> dropping the need for a config.json file altogether. Running only on ENV\n> vars is perfectly feasible, and pretty easy with viper.\n>\n> I am closing this PR, and will think on a better way to implement this.\n>\n> —\n> You are receiving this because you commented.\n> Reply to this email directly, view it on GitHub\n> <https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/57#issuecomment-886225510>,\n> or unsubscribe\n> <https://github.com/notifications/unsubscribe-au